# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: bricscad-v25-metric-template-stays-booting -- BricsCAD V25 (Windows) never reaches READY on a copy of Default-m.dwt
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-25

* Symptom

probe:template-defaults:bricscad-metric:windows (job 17450398554, PF5S26B,
BricsCAD V25 fr_FR): alfe opens a copy of
AppData/Local/Bricsys/BricsCAD/V25x64/fr_FR/Templates/Default-m.dwt (named
template.dwg, via $AUTOLISP_DWG) and the runtime never gets past BOOTING:
READY timeout after 180 s, launcher exit 0, engine killed, exit 75.

The same job on Default-imperial.dwt (job 17449031340) reached READY and
finished in under 20 s; BricsCAD V26 macOS on its Default-m.dwt (job
17449031343) completed too. (The job's 12m45s template lookup, first taken
for an alfe timeout that did not fire, was run-probes.sh's -- fixed with
alfe-batch-timeout-not-enforced.)

* Suspects

A modal dialog BricsCAD V25 raises while opening that file before
run-common.lsp loads (missing font / xref / proxy, a units or recovery
prompt): cf. alfe-cad-nil-catch-all-message, empty-ressource. alfe's batch
mode cannot see it.

* To do

1. Retry the job once (the first run may have been a cold-start artefact).
2. If it reproduces: look at the runner's screen during the READY wait, or
   open the copy by hand in BricsCAD V25 on PF5S26B.
3. Once it runs: its set goes into cador's default objects as
   (:bricscad :metric 25) (MR !489 falls back to V26's).
